.build/
.swiftpm/
*.xcodeproj
*.xcworkspace
DerivedData/

# The recorded corpus lives in Fixtures/ and IS committed. It was local-only while the
# scrubber let real content through: multipart request bodies bypassed scrubbing entirely, so
# form fields carrying an address were written verbatim, and link-local IPv6 addresses (which
# embed the interface MAC) and absolute /Users/<name> paths in stack traces were never
# touched. All three are scrubbed now, and the corpus was re-scrubbed and audited before
# being committed. See docs/api/README.md.
#
# If you record against a live server, RE-AUDIT before pushing; the scrubber is a filter, not
# a guarantee, and it has been wrong before.

# The chat.db fixtures are COMMITTED, not ignored. They named a directory that has
# never existed (`Tests/ChatDBFixtures`), so this rule matched nothing and the prose
# built on it was wrong in both directions. The generator is deterministic and its
# self-test proves byte-identical regeneration, so committing them keeps `swift test`
# free of a Python dependency. See .claude/docs/workflow.md.

# Bytecode from the Python checkers and generators under Tools/. Every one of them is run
# as `python3 Tools/<tool>/<script>.py`, so a local run of what CI checks leaves these
# behind next to the scripts.
__pycache__/

# Repository-wide noise, inherited from the layout before the Swift server became the
# root: editor state, Finder droppings, stray logs, and the local .env that carries the
# live-send test addresses (see CONTRIBUTING.md § "Test data: never real addresses").
.vscode
.DS_Store
**/*.log
.env

# Reference implementations, installed locally to generate protocol vectors.
Tools/protocol-vectors/node_modules/
Tools/protocol-vectors/package-lock.json

# Local state from `wrangler dev` under Tools/licence-worker: a miniflare cache and its
# KV store, written on every local run. Machine-local and not reproducible, and it was
# swept into the index once by a `git add -A` during the repository restructure.
.wrangler/

# The observation probe is a separate package with its own build directory.
Tools/observation-probe/.build/
